title: Reconcile
tags: [[File tracking]]
kind: overview
summary: Reconcile walks the tree on demand: it creates what is missing, recognises moved files by their content, refreshes what changed — and never marks a file deleted.

The watcher records what happens while the daemon runs; ''reconcile'' makes the store
agree with the disk after the fact. It walks the repository — pruned by eligibility and
by offline mount points ([[Offline subtrees]]) — and, in one revision:

* ''creates'' a metarecord for every eligible file and directory that has none;
* recognises files that ''moved'' while nobody watched, by their content fingerprint, and follows them ([[Moves and candidates]]);
* ''refreshes'' the stat fields of what is still in place, catching edits made while the watcher was off;
* fills in the MIME type and the embedded metadata of files that lack them.

It runs when you ask ([[Running a reconcile]]) — after setting `mf_watch` on a folder,
after the daemon was down, after a broker gap — and never on its own.

What it never does: set `mfr_path` to `nothing`. A metarecord whose file is not where
it was keeps its stale path; only the watcher, which ''saw'' the deletion, may say a
file is gone. A stale path is an orphan to relink, or to clear, deliberately (`mf orphan`).

